---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CliSidebar from '../../../components/CliSidebar.astro';
---

<Layout title="Command Reference - MEDE-CLI">
  <div class="docs-layout">
    <CliSidebar />
    <article class="docs-content prose">
      <h1>Command Reference</h1>
      
      <p>
        MEDE-CLI is operated using specific commands. Every documentation change undergoes a transactional cycle: proposal ➡️ approval/refinement ➡️ application.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Cycle Commands</h2>

      <h3><code>mede cycle [-p prompt] [-f file]</code></h3>
      <p>Initiates a new documentation evolution cycle or advances the current phase. If it is the first cycle of the project, it generates the Meeting Minutes based on the provided context.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>-p, --prompt</code>: Additional text context supplied directly in the command line.</li>
        <li><code>-f, --file</code>: Path to a file containing text context (useful for raw meeting notes or transcripts).</li>
      </ul>

      <h3><code>mede status</code></h3>
      <p>Inspects and prints the current operational state of the cycle. Displays the active phase, active language, which files have been modified, and available terminal actions.</p>

      <h3><code>mede approve [-a]</code></h3>
      <p>Approves the LLM-generated proposal for the current phase and advances the cycle to the next stage.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>-a, --auto</code>: Auto-approves all remaining phases in the cycle continuously.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3><code>mede reject [-a]</code></h3>
      <p>Rejects the LLM-generated proposal for the current phase.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Special behavior for Meeting Minutes:</strong> Rejecting the first phase (Meeting Minutes) cancels the entire cycle. For other phases, rejecting simply skips that phase, allowing the cycle to proceed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3><code>mede refine [-p prompt] [-f file]</code></h3>
      <p>Requests the LLM to rewrite the proposal for the current phase, incorporating the provided text observations or corrections.</p>

      <h3><code>mede commit</code></h3>
      <p>Finalizes the current cycle. Commits and consolidates all proposed changes to the disk, cleaning up temporary snapshots.</p>

      <h3><code>mede rollback</code></h3>
      <p>Cancels the current cycle entirely and restores all live documents to their pre-cycle state, removing any newly created files in the process.</p>

      <h2>2. Chunk (Diff) Commands</h2>

      <h3><code>mede pending</code></h3>
      <p>Lists all generated diff chunks (change-chunks) awaiting action (status <code>PENDING</code>).</p>

      <h3><code>mede apply [-a]</code></h3>
      <p>Applies the current pending diff chunk to the actual live document.</p>

      <h3><code>mede discard [-a]</code></h3>
      <p>Discards the current pending diff chunk, marking it as discarded without applying the changes.</p>

      <h2>3. Utilities</h2>

      <h3><code>mede diff &lt;file&gt;</code></h3>
      <p>Shows the visual diff (colored red/green) between the original snapshot and the suggested changes for the specified file.</p>

      <h3><code>mede files</code></h3>
      <p>Lists all files that have been modified or created during the current cycle.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
